<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?><rss version="2.0" xmlns:content="http://purl.org/rss/1.0/modules/content/"><channel><title>Ross Churchley</title><description>A field notebook, kept in the open</description><link>https://rosschurchley.com/</link><item><title>Photo of the day for 2026-09-17</title><link>https://rosschurchley.com/2026/birds-duck-formation/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://rosschurchley.com/2026/birds-duck-formation/</guid><pubDate>Thu, 17 Sep 2026 23:12:00 GMT</pubDate><content:encoded>&lt;figure&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;/_astro/src.B9DKig58_Zoq5gs.webp&quot; width=1086 height=724 alt=Two male mallards, two female mallards, and one bufflehead duck swim in formation along a pond.&gt;&lt;/figure&gt;</content:encoded></item><item><title>Photo of the day for 2026-09-16</title><link>https://rosschurchley.com/2026/birds-gull-food/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://rosschurchley.com/2026/birds-gull-food/</guid><pubDate>Wed, 16 Sep 2026 23:12:00 GMT</pubDate><content:encoded>&lt;figure&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;/_astro/src.DNELhIJl_26OIpJ.webp&quot; width=1086 height=724 alt=An immature gull in flight carries a bit of food in its beak.&gt;&lt;/figure&gt;</content:encoded></item><item><title>Photo of the day for 2026-09-15</title><link>https://rosschurchley.com/2026/birds-crow-sunning/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://rosschurchley.com/2026/birds-crow-sunning/</guid><pubDate>Tue, 15 Sep 2026 23:12:00 GMT</pubDate><content:encoded>&lt;figure&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;/_astro/src.B7DLw_tP_2nv7X3.webp&quot; width=6000 height=4000 alt=A crow with an open beak spreads its body on a grass lawn to sun itself.&gt;&lt;/figure&gt;</content:encoded></item><item><title>Tillicum the Otter</title><link>https://rosschurchley.com/2026/tillicum/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://rosschurchley.com/2026/tillicum/</guid><pubDate>Mon, 14 Sep 2026 23:12:00 GMT</pubDate><content:encoded>&lt;figure&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;/_astro/cover.0QbzIYSP_1NdVej.webp&quot; width=5376 height=3630 alt=Tillicum in property tax lineup at Vancouver City Hall (Vancouver Archives item 2011-010.379)&gt;&lt;/figure&gt;&lt;p&gt;Vancouver’s centennial celebrations had a mascot: Tillicum the sea otter. (Interestingly, only river otters are native to the Vancouver area, but sea otters are a big part of BC coastal history.)&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The &lt;a href=&quot;https://searcharchives.vancouver.ca&quot;&gt;Vancouver Archives&lt;/a&gt; has a ton of hilarious &lt;a href=&quot;https://searcharchives.vancouver.ca/informationobject/browse?subjects=2689126&amp;amp;topLod=0&amp;amp;sort=relevance&amp;amp;query=tillicum&amp;amp;sq0=tillicum&amp;amp;sortDir=desc&quot;&gt;photos of Tillicum&lt;/a&gt;. Here are a few of my favourites:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;figure&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;gallery-grid&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;gallery-item&quot;&gt;  &lt;img src=&quot;/_astro/bowling.jPVmEx2M_Z1eiYUO.webp&quot; srcset=&quot;/_astro/bowling.jPVmEx2M_Z1R8EEt.webp 640w, /_astro/bowling.jPVmEx2M_1rEyac.webp 750w, /_astro/bowling.jPVmEx2M_28kS9v.webp 828w, /_astro/bowling.jPVmEx2M_EqpJw.webp 1080w, /_astro/bowling.jPVmEx2M_n44h7.webp 1280w, /_astro/bowling.jPVmEx2M_5p2N0.webp 1668w&quot; alt=&quot;Tillicum and a group dressed as bowling pins and a bowling ball - don’t ask me why&quot; loading=&quot;lazy&quot; decoding=&quot;async&quot; sizes=&quot;100vw&quot; data-astro-image=&quot;full-width&quot; data-astro-image-fit=&quot;cover&quot; data-astro-image-pos=&quot;center&quot; width=&quot;2012&quot; height=&quot;3000&quot; class=&quot;gallery-item__image&quot;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;gallery-item&quot;&gt;  &lt;img src=&quot;/_astro/diana.C1yjrJAH_Z2sstwg.webp&quot; srcset=&quot;/_astro/diana.C1yjrJAH_Z2uqRXX.webp 640w, /_astro/diana.C1yjrJAH_1yRpTP.webp 750w, /_astro/diana.C1yjrJAH_1h3XRD.webp 828w, /_astro/diana.C1yjrJAH_Z1iDMCp.webp 1080w, /_astro/diana.C1yjrJAH_CbBJC.webp 1280w, /_astro/diana.C1yjrJAH_fbVEN.webp 1668w&quot; alt=&quot;Tillicum standing beside Prince Charles and Princess Diana cutouts&quot; loading=&quot;lazy&quot; decoding=&quot;async&quot; sizes=&quot;100vw&quot; data-astro-image=&quot;full-width&quot; data-astro-image-fit=&quot;cover&quot; data-astro-image-pos=&quot;center&quot; width=&quot;2019&quot; height=&quot;3000&quot; class=&quot;gallery-item__image&quot;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;gallery-item&quot;&gt;  &lt;img src=&quot;/_astro/phone.BmK4MA0V_ZdkFqg.webp&quot; srcset=&quot;/_astro/phone.BmK4MA0V_1eA3P9.webp 640w, /_astro/phone.BmK4MA0V_Z2l5xYT.webp 750w, /_astro/phone.BmK4MA0V_S7McA.webp 828w, /_astro/phone.BmK4MA0V_ZvdoEv.webp 1080w, /_astro/phone.BmK4MA0V_Z9kF5l.webp 1280w, /_astro/phone.BmK4MA0V_1KtH6K.webp 1668w, /_astro/phone.BmK4MA0V_25i2aL.webp 2048w, /_astro/phone.BmK4MA0V_ZvmBNV.webp 2560w&quot; alt=&quot;Tillicum on the telephone at an office desk in Vancouver City Hall&quot; loading=&quot;lazy&quot; decoding=&quot;async&quot; sizes=&quot;100vw&quot; data-astro-image=&quot;full-width&quot; data-astro-image-fit=&quot;cover&quot; data-astro-image-pos=&quot;center&quot; width=&quot;5322&quot; height=&quot;3636&quot; class=&quot;gallery-item__image&quot;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;gallery-item&quot;&gt;  &lt;img src=&quot;/_astro/mayor.DlxBcaQE_vShqK.webp&quot; srcset=&quot;/_astro/mayor.DlxBcaQE_F5uFH.webp 640w, /_astro/mayor.DlxBcaQE_Z2api7G.webp 750w, /_astro/mayor.DlxBcaQE_17TzlA.webp 828w, /_astro/mayor.DlxBcaQE_2uJrtb.webp 1080w, /_astro/mayor.DlxBcaQE_1mbiTz.webp 1280w, /_astro/mayor.DlxBcaQE_Z1AtO2A.webp 1668w, /_astro/mayor.DlxBcaQE_Z2beOII.webp 2048w, /_astro/mayor.DlxBcaQE_uYhKb.webp 2560w&quot; alt=&quot;Mayor Harcourt delivering speech with Tillicum in background&quot; loading=&quot;lazy&quot; decoding=&quot;async&quot; sizes=&quot;100vw&quot; data-astro-image=&quot;full-width&quot; data-astro-image-fit=&quot;cover&quot; data-astro-image-pos=&quot;center&quot; width=&quot;5335&quot; height=&quot;3583&quot; class=&quot;gallery-item__image&quot;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;figcaption&gt;Photos of Tillicum from the Vancouver Archives (&lt;a href=&quot;https://searcharchives.vancouver.ca/tillicum-and-group-dressed-as-bowling-pins-and-bowling-ball-4&quot;&gt;1&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://searcharchives.vancouver.ca/tillicum-standing-beside-prince-charles-and-princess-diana-cutouts&quot;&gt;2&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://searcharchives.vancouver.ca/tillicum-on-telephone-at-office-desk-in-vancouver-city-hall-3&quot;&gt;3&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://searcharchives.vancouver.ca/mayor-harcourt-delivering-speech-with-tillicum-in-background&quot;&gt;4&lt;/a&gt;)&lt;/figcaption&gt;&lt;/figure&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The name Tillicum means “friend” or “people” in the &lt;a href=&quot;https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chinook_Jargon&quot;&gt;Chinook Jargon&lt;/a&gt;, a pidgin language used to mediate trade between white settlers and First Nations. Chinook words were then &lt;a href=&quot;https://dx.doi.org/10.14288/1.0433567&quot;&gt;considered the safe choice&lt;/a&gt; for naming things without a specific First Nation gifting a name; at the time, &lt;a href=&quot;https://vancouver.ca/people-programs/vancouvers-journey-towards-reconciliation.aspx&quot;&gt;reconciliation&lt;/a&gt; had not yet begun.&lt;/p&gt;</content:encoded></item><item><title>Photo of the day for 2026-09-14</title><link>https://rosschurchley.com/2026/birds-parrots/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://rosschurchley.com/2026/birds-parrots/</guid><pubDate>Mon, 14 Sep 2026 23:12:00 GMT</pubDate><content:encoded>&lt;figure&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;/_astro/src.BS-aAiU3_ZCPem0.webp&quot; width=1024 height=768 alt=A pair of blue parrots feed from a bowl over a shallow koi-filled pond.&gt;&lt;/figure&gt;</content:encoded></item><item><title>Photo of the day for 2026-09-13</title><link>https://rosschurchley.com/2026/birds-goose-splashdown/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://rosschurchley.com/2026/birds-goose-splashdown/</guid><pubDate>Sun, 13 Sep 2026 23:12:00 GMT</pubDate><content:encoded>&lt;figure&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;/_astro/src.DGI63kRk_Z1Oxz6C.webp&quot; width=6000 height=4000 alt=A Canada goose with outstretched wings splashes down into a pond.&gt;&lt;/figure&gt;</content:encoded></item><item><title>Photo of the day for 2026-09-12</title><link>https://rosschurchley.com/2026/moon-eclipse/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://rosschurchley.com/2026/moon-eclipse/</guid><pubDate>Sat, 12 Sep 2026 23:12:00 GMT</pubDate><content:encoded>&lt;figure&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;/_astro/src.JiaYtzPB_Z1UmCsg.webp&quot; width=6000 height=4000 alt=A partially-eclipsed moon behind the faint silhouette of leaves&gt;&lt;/figure&gt;</content:encoded></item><item><title>Photo of the day for 2026-09-11</title><link>https://rosschurchley.com/2026/moon-dragon/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://rosschurchley.com/2026/moon-dragon/</guid><pubDate>Fri, 11 Sep 2026 23:12:00 GMT</pubDate><content:encoded>&lt;figure&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;/_astro/src.jp2XJPhH_Z1Oy1N3.webp&quot; width=3072 height=2304 alt=A statue of a dragon with an open mouth appearing to bite the crescent moon&gt;&lt;/figure&gt;</content:encoded></item><item><title>Photo of the day for 2026-09-10</title><link>https://rosschurchley.com/2026/moon-crescent/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://rosschurchley.com/2026/moon-crescent/</guid><pubDate>Thu, 10 Sep 2026 23:12:00 GMT</pubDate><content:encoded>&lt;figure&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;/_astro/src.B_POKjOO_fCDu5.webp&quot; width=6000 height=4000 alt=The crescent moon in a denim blue sky&gt;&lt;/figure&gt;</content:encoded></item><item><title>Photo of the day for 2026-09-09</title><link>https://rosschurchley.com/2026/moon-cn-tower/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://rosschurchley.com/2026/moon-cn-tower/</guid><pubDate>Wed, 09 Sep 2026 23:12:00 GMT</pubDate><content:encoded>&lt;figure&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;/_astro/src.BwikxX4b_Z1ssEe.webp&quot; width=1680 height=2240 alt=The moon at dusk is framed by trees and a distant CN tower&gt;&lt;/figure&gt;</content:encoded></item><item><title>Photo of the day for 2026-09-08</title><link>https://rosschurchley.com/2026/moon-plane/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://rosschurchley.com/2026/moon-plane/</guid><pubDate>Tue, 08 Sep 2026 23:12:00 GMT</pubDate><content:encoded>&lt;figure&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;/_astro/src.C1elGDTT_ZmAYrd.webp&quot; width=4754 height=2674 alt=A plane passes in front of a quarter-moon&gt;&lt;/figure&gt;</content:encoded></item><item><title>Allspice is one spice</title><link>https://rosschurchley.com/2026/allspice-is-one-spice/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://rosschurchley.com/2026/allspice-is-one-spice/</guid><pubDate>Mon, 07 Sep 2026 23:12:00 GMT</pubDate><content:encoded>&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Allspice&quot;&gt;Allspice&lt;/a&gt; is just one spice, namely the dried fruit of the &lt;em&gt;Pimenta dioica&lt;/em&gt; plant. It’s called allspice because the English thought it combined the flavours of cinnamon, nutmeg, and clove.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;There’s an obvious joke in there about English cooking, so I fact-checked it. While the average 17th-century village shop only offered four spices, well-stocked grocers &lt;a href=&quot;https://bura.brunel.ac.uk/handle/2438/31460&quot;&gt;had up to nineteen&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;</content:encoded></item><item><title>Photo of the day for 2026-09-07</title><link>https://rosschurchley.com/2026/moon-batchelor/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://rosschurchley.com/2026/moon-batchelor/</guid><pubDate>Mon, 07 Sep 2026 23:12:00 GMT</pubDate><content:encoded>&lt;figure&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;/_astro/src.Dwn6-28C_Z1iTpV1.webp&quot; width=1536 height=2048 alt=The crescent moon hovers over a fully-silhouetted house on a hill.&gt;&lt;/figure&gt;</content:encoded></item><item><title>Photo of the day for 2026-09-06</title><link>https://rosschurchley.com/2026/moon-moondog/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://rosschurchley.com/2026/moon-moondog/</guid><pubDate>Sun, 06 Sep 2026 23:12:00 GMT</pubDate><content:encoded>&lt;figure&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;/_astro/src.CqNLJ2zX_Z1d8Bn8.webp&quot; width=6000 height=4000 alt=A partially-eclipsed moon illuminates a halo of clouds&gt;&lt;/figure&gt;</content:encoded></item><item><title>Kulshan from Oak Bay at sunset</title><link>https://rosschurchley.com/2026/painting-kulshan/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://rosschurchley.com/2026/painting-kulshan/</guid><pubDate>Sat, 14 Feb 2026 23:12:00 GMT</pubDate><content:encoded>&lt;figure&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;/_astro/cover.2eiorcZP_2nYg5b.webp&quot; width=3636 height=2727 alt=A brightly-coloured painting depicting a distant mountain under a purple, red, and pink sky.&gt;&lt;/figure&gt;&lt;p&gt;I’m continuing to experiment with different paint media and styles. This piece is gouache on laser cut wood. The composition is based on a photo I took back in 2007, and the style was inspired by an &lt;a href=&quot;https://bellamyhomestudio.com/collections/diy/products/paint-by-number-art-kit-howe-sound-squamish&quot;&gt;art kit from Meghan Bellamy&lt;/a&gt; I recently did.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;figure&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;gallery-grid&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;gallery-item&quot;&gt;  &lt;img src=&quot;/_astro/C615C1F4-6B7B-45B4-80D7-47F52C93538F_1_105_c.D-G548nY_70izS.webp&quot; srcset=&quot;/_astro/C615C1F4-6B7B-45B4-80D7-47F52C93538F_1_105_c.D-G548nY_2roF6o.webp 640w, /_astro/C615C1F4-6B7B-45B4-80D7-47F52C93538F_1_105_c.D-G548nY_Z1ngPrx.webp 750w&quot; alt=&quot;A photo of Kulshan (Mount Baker) at sunset from across the Juan de Fuca Strait&quot; loading=&quot;lazy&quot; decoding=&quot;async&quot; sizes=&quot;100vw&quot; data-astro-image=&quot;full-width&quot; data-astro-image-fit=&quot;cover&quot; data-astro-image-pos=&quot;center&quot; width=&quot;768&quot; height=&quot;1024&quot; class=&quot;gallery-item__image&quot;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;gallery-item&quot;&gt;  &lt;img src=&quot;/_astro/IMG_2565.DIbkVIqP_ZaSF7i.webp&quot; srcset=&quot;/_astro/IMG_2565.DIbkVIqP_Z1bMQ2M.webp 640w, /_astro/IMG_2565.DIbkVIqP_15HKR1.webp 750w, /_astro/IMG_2565.DIbkVIqP_Z2s8c4g.webp 828w, /_astro/IMG_2565.DIbkVIqP_1qpxbO.webp 1080w, /_astro/IMG_2565.DIbkVIqP_rn838.webp 1280w, /_astro/IMG_2565.DIbkVIqP_ZryMMk.webp 1668w, /_astro/IMG_2565.DIbkVIqP_1xj87q.webp 2048w, /_astro/IMG_2565.DIbkVIqP_Z2hFCct.webp 2560w&quot; alt=&quot;An abstract watercolour-on-wood painting of Átl’ḵa7tsem (Howe Sound) based on a design by Meghan Bellamy&quot; loading=&quot;lazy&quot; decoding=&quot;async&quot; sizes=&quot;100vw&quot; data-astro-image=&quot;full-width&quot; data-astro-image-fit=&quot;cover&quot; data-astro-image-pos=&quot;center&quot; width=&quot;2814&quot; height=&quot;3482&quot; class=&quot;gallery-item__image&quot;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/figure&gt;</content:encoded></item><item><title>Photo of the day for 2025-07-12</title><link>https://rosschurchley.com/2025/trains-canada-line-marine/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://rosschurchley.com/2025/trains-canada-line-marine/</guid><pubDate>Sat, 12 Jul 2025 23:12:00 GMT</pubDate><content:encoded>&lt;figure&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;/_astro/src.C3cHO_wy_Z19HL2f.webp&quot; width=6000 height=4000 alt=A pair of blue and silver trains travel along a curved elevated railway track.&gt;&lt;/figure&gt;</content:encoded></item><item><title>Photo of the day for 2025-07-11</title><link>https://rosschurchley.com/2025/trains-canada-line-tunnel/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://rosschurchley.com/2025/trains-canada-line-tunnel/</guid><pubDate>Fri, 11 Jul 2025 23:12:00 GMT</pubDate><content:encoded>&lt;figure&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;/_astro/src.DlIj3h96_ZXPLsY.webp&quot; width=6000 height=4000 alt=An empty subway tunnel extends into the distance. The closest part of the tunnel is illuminated by a blue LED or a blacklight. The rest of the tunnel has white lights spaced at intervals.&gt;&lt;/figure&gt;</content:encoded></item><item><title>Photo of the day for 2025-07-10</title><link>https://rosschurchley.com/2025/trains-skytrain-raindrops/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://rosschurchley.com/2025/trains-skytrain-raindrops/</guid><pubDate>Thu, 10 Jul 2025 23:12:00 GMT</pubDate><content:encoded>&lt;figure&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;/_astro/src.BJMartHf_oiHSR.webp&quot; width=1936 height=2592 alt=Raindrops streak down a window, obscuring a view of the train tracks ahead. The light suggests that the sun may be setting soon in clearer skies to the right of frame.&gt;&lt;/figure&gt;</content:encoded></item><item><title>Photo of the day for 2025-07-09</title><link>https://rosschurchley.com/2025/trains-dc-metro/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://rosschurchley.com/2025/trains-dc-metro/</guid><pubDate>Wed, 09 Jul 2025 23:12:00 GMT</pubDate><content:encoded>&lt;figure&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;/_astro/src.B_ZzbU77_ZNDzFw.webp&quot; width=3264 height=2448 alt=A subway train is stopped at a platform. Red lights mark the edge of the platform, and the elliptical ceiling is half-illuminated.&gt;&lt;/figure&gt;</content:encoded></item><item><title>Photo of the day for 2025-07-08</title><link>https://rosschurchley.com/2025/trains-model/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://rosschurchley.com/2025/trains-model/</guid><pubDate>Tue, 08 Jul 2025 23:12:00 GMT</pubDate><content:encoded>&lt;figure&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;/_astro/src.CkGJktHM_2f9BAu.webp&quot; width=6000 height=4000 alt=A model train on an elevated track passes a green signal light.&gt;&lt;/figure&gt;</content:encoded></item><item><title>Photo of the day for 2025-07-07</title><link>https://rosschurchley.com/2025/trains-antique-shinkansen/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://rosschurchley.com/2025/trains-antique-shinkansen/</guid><pubDate>Mon, 07 Jul 2025 23:12:00 GMT</pubDate><content:encoded>&lt;figure&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;/_astro/src.Dl7j36pl_1GuCMP.webp&quot; width=6000 height=4000 alt=Spacious seats in the interior of an original 1960s bullet train.&gt;&lt;/figure&gt;</content:encoded></item><item><title>Photo of the day for 2025-07-06</title><link>https://rosschurchley.com/2025/trains-vanishing-point/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://rosschurchley.com/2025/trains-vanishing-point/</guid><pubDate>Sun, 06 Jul 2025 23:12:00 GMT</pubDate><content:encoded>&lt;figure&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;/_astro/src.uDVVK4O6_13FOlr.webp&quot; width=3024 height=4032 alt=A pair of train tracks and overhead wires run straight past a platform and into the distance.&gt;&lt;/figure&gt;</content:encoded></item><item><title>Photo of the day for 2025-05-17</title><link>https://rosschurchley.com/2025/birds-blue-crow/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://rosschurchley.com/2025/birds-blue-crow/</guid><pubDate>Sat, 17 May 2025 23:12:00 GMT</pubDate><content:encoded>&lt;figure&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;/_astro/src.BazyBm_P_xJFTE.webp&quot; width=3872 height=2592 alt=A crow perches on a thin branch against a bright blue sky.&gt;&lt;/figure&gt;</content:encoded></item><item><title>Photo of the day for 2025-05-16</title><link>https://rosschurchley.com/2025/birds-baby-castle-pigeon/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://rosschurchley.com/2025/birds-baby-castle-pigeon/</guid><pubDate>Fri, 16 May 2025 23:12:00 GMT</pubDate><content:encoded>&lt;figure&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;/_astro/src.C6FbyQDs_Z1DiHsc.webp&quot; width=2304 height=3072 alt=A tiny, fluffy bird stands on a glass surface next to a stone wall.&gt;&lt;/figure&gt;</content:encoded></item><item><title>Photo of the day for 2025-05-15</title><link>https://rosschurchley.com/2025/birds-pne-crows/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://rosschurchley.com/2025/birds-pne-crows/</guid><pubDate>Thu, 15 May 2025 23:12:00 GMT</pubDate><content:encoded>&lt;figure&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;/_astro/src.BqjHvRGr_20lL2Y.webp&quot; width=6000 height=4000 alt=A flock of crows populate the trees in front of a red and white tower.&gt;&lt;/figure&gt;</content:encoded></item><item><title>Photo of the day for 2025-05-14</title><link>https://rosschurchley.com/2025/birds-eagle-looking-up/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://rosschurchley.com/2025/birds-eagle-looking-up/</guid><pubDate>Wed, 14 May 2025 23:12:00 GMT</pubDate><content:encoded>&lt;figure&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;/_astro/src.B_0_4Oli_1PPkxg.webp&quot; width=3872 height=2592 alt=A bald eagle looks intently upwards. The bird&apos;s profile is framed by out-of-focus green leaves.&gt;&lt;/figure&gt;</content:encoded></item><item><title>Photo of the day for 2025-05-13</title><link>https://rosschurchley.com/2025/birds-kamloops-flock/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://rosschurchley.com/2025/birds-kamloops-flock/</guid><pubDate>Tue, 13 May 2025 23:12:00 GMT</pubDate><content:encoded>&lt;figure&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;/_astro/src.I6YhRgCy_Z25mrls.webp&quot; width=2048 height=1536 alt=Several birds fly across a blue sky over a tree-lined street.&gt;&lt;/figure&gt;</content:encoded></item><item><title>Photo of the day for 2025-05-12</title><link>https://rosschurchley.com/2025/birds-sleeping-duck/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://rosschurchley.com/2025/birds-sleeping-duck/</guid><pubDate>Mon, 12 May 2025 23:12:00 GMT<