no-tree/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://rosschurchley.com/2025/mountains-tofino-tree/</guid><pubDate>Thu, 08 May 2025 23:12:00 GMT</pubDate><content:encoded>&lt;figure&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;/_astro/src.D9aUWmAO_ZBvKiL.webp&quot; width=3726 height=2493 alt=A lone tree stands atop a rocky cliff overlooking the ocean. Waves lap against the base of the cliff under a bright sky.&gt;&lt;/figure&gt;</content:encoded></item><item><title>Photo of the day for 2025-05-07</title><link>https://rosschurchley.com/2025/mountains-sunset-seagull/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://rosschurchley.com/2025/mountains-sunset-seagull/</guid><pubDate>Wed, 07 May 2025 23:12:00 GMT</pubDate><content:encoded>&lt;figure&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;/_astro/src.BuDztEt7_1qMolV.webp&quot; width=3872 height=2178 alt=A bird soars over a calm body of water with snow-capped mountains in the distance. The sunset sky is a mix of orange and blue.&gt;&lt;/figure&gt;</content:encoded></item><item><title>Photo of the day for 2025-05-06</title><link>https://rosschurchley.com/2025/mountains-rockies/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://rosschurchley.com/2025/mountains-rockies/</guid><pubDate>Tue, 06 May 2025 23:12:00 GMT</pubDate><content:encoded>&lt;figure&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;/_astro/src.B0R4lcJl_Z1kIJFk.webp&quot; width=1536 height=2048 alt=A snow-covered mountain viewed from above. White clouds partially obscure the peak.&gt;&lt;/figure&gt;</content:encoded></item><item><title>Photo of the day for 2025-05-05</title><link>https://rosschurchley.com/2025/mountains-kamloops-xp/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://rosschurchley.com/2025/mountains-kamloops-xp/</guid><pubDate>Mon, 05 May 2025 23:12:00 GMT</pubDate><content:encoded>&lt;figure&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;/_astro/src.DIBlnBYJ_wOQnT.webp&quot; width=6000 height=4000 alt= A sagebrush-covered hill rises against a clear blue sky.&gt;&lt;/figure&gt;</content:encoded></item><item><title>Photo of the day for 2025-05-04</title><link>https://rosschurchley.com/2025/mountains-rockies-inukshuk/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://rosschurchley.com/2025/mountains-rockies-inukshuk/</guid><pubDate>Sun, 04 May 2025 23:12:00 GMT</pubDate><content:encoded>&lt;figure&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;/_astro/src.Bbrft6EY_NrP03.webp&quot; width=1679 height=1678 alt=An inukshuk on a rocky outcrop with a backdrop of snow-covered mountains under a cloudy sky.&gt;&lt;/figure&gt;</content:encoded></item><item><title>Photo of the day for 2025-05-03</title><link>https://rosschurchley.com/2025/construction-kenrokuen-tree-ropes/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://rosschurchley.com/2025/construction-kenrokuen-tree-ropes/</guid><pubDate>Sat, 03 May 2025 23:12:00 GMT</pubDate><content:encoded>&lt;figure&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;/_astro/src.CAsaMxMh_ZKPjek.webp&quot; width=6000 height=4000 alt=A helmeted Japanese worker in the branches of a pine tree looks upwards. Many ropes are suspended from a tall pole out of frame and are being tied to the tree&apos;s branches for support.&gt;&lt;/figure&gt;</content:encoded></item><item><title>Photo of the day for 2025-05-02</title><link>https://rosschurchley.com/2025/construction-hillside/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://rosschurchley.com/2025/construction-hillside/</guid><pubDate>Fri, 02 May 2025 23:12:00 GMT</pubDate><content:encoded>&lt;figure&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;/_astro/src.CKqswL26_twfxu.webp&quot; width=6000 height=4000 alt=Metal posts secured with cables support a grassy hillside, for erosion control or earthquake preparedness.&gt;&lt;/figure&gt;</content:encoded></item><item><title>Photo of the day for 2025-05-01</title><link>https://rosschurchley.com/2025/construction-power-station/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://rosschurchley.com/2025/construction-power-station/</guid><pubDate>Thu, 01 May 2025 23:12:00 GMT</pubDate><content:encoded>&lt;figure&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;/_astro/src.Gi86g7ff_ZRB3u5.webp&quot; width=3741 height=2806 alt=A large rectangular concrete building sits on the water at the base of a forested mountain.&gt;&lt;/figure&gt;</content:encoded></item><item><title>Photo of the day for 2025-04-30</title><link>https://rosschurchley.com/2025/construction-post/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://rosschurchley.com/2025/construction-post/</guid><pubDate>Wed, 30 Apr 2025 23:12:00 GMT</pubDate><content:encoded>&lt;figure&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;/_astro/src.CV9zgihR_ZK4JYh.webp&quot; width=6000 height=4000 alt=A metal post is driven into a mossy rock with the blue water of Burrard Inlet in the background.&gt;&lt;/figure&gt;</content:encoded></item><item><title>Photo of the day for 2025-04-29</title><link>https://rosschurchley.com/2025/construction-church/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://rosschurchley.com/2025/construction-church/</guid><pubDate>Tue, 29 Apr 2025 23:12:00 GMT</pubDate><content:encoded>&lt;figure&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;/_astro/src.Bsi-K8jx_ZoRkN2.webp&quot; width=3072 height=2304 alt=A stone church tower is being repaired with scaffolding, while a modern glass skyscraper is being constructed in the background.&gt;&lt;/figure&gt;</content:encoded></item><item><title>Photo of the day for 2025-04-28</title><link>https://rosschurchley.com/2025/construction-drainage/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://rosschurchley.com/2025/construction-drainage/</guid><pubDate>Mon, 28 Apr 2025 23:12:00 GMT</pubDate><content:encoded>&lt;figure&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;/_astro/src.BJxBr4nZ_iqu04.webp&quot; width=5893 height=3315 alt=Inside a small drainage channel filled with water and debris. The channel&apos;s metal walls are textured with ridges.&gt;&lt;/figure&gt;</content:encoded></item><item><title>Photo of the day for 2025-04-27</title><link>https://rosschurchley.com/2025/construction-crane/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://rosschurchley.com/2025/construction-crane/</guid><pubDate>Sun, 27 Apr 2025 23:12:00 GMT</pubDate><content:encoded>&lt;figure&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;/_astro/src.D6NGCxBB_klRUW.webp&quot; width=6000 height=4000 alt=A yellow tower crane rises against a partly cloudy sky, with the focus on the operator&apos;s cab.&gt;&lt;/figure&gt;</content:encoded></item><item><title>Photo of the day for 2025-04-19</title><link>https://rosschurchley.com/2025/animals-grazing-cow/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://rosschurchley.com/2025/animals-grazing-cow/</guid><pubDate>Sat, 19 Apr 2025 23:12:00 GMT</pubDate><content:encoded>&lt;figure&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;/_astro/src.CH4NN3io_1GCyj8.webp&quot; width=6000 height=4000 alt=A black cow grazes in a field, lowering its head to eat grass.&gt;&lt;/figure&gt;</content:encoded></item><item><title>Photo of the day for 2025-04-18</title><link>https://rosschurchley.com/2025/animals-winter-horses/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://rosschurchley.com/2025/animals-winter-horses/</guid><pubDate>Fri, 18 Apr 2025 23:12:00 GMT</pubDate><content:encoded>&lt;figure&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;/_astro/src.lveHum-e_ZUXd0F.webp&quot; width=6000 height=4000 alt=Two horses stand together in a field. One is brown, and the other has a spotted coat. The ground is covered in frost, and a forest of bare beech trees is in the background.&gt;&lt;/figure&gt;</content:encoded></item><item><title>Photo of the day for 2025-04-17</title><link>https://rosschurchley.com/2025/animals-turtle-gathering/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://rosschurchley.com/2025/animals-turtle-gathering/</guid><pubDate>Thu, 17 Apr 2025 23:12:00 GMT</pubDate><content:encoded>&lt;figure&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;/_astro/src.CG1Gj1-M_Z1LXf6H.webp&quot; width=6000 height=4000 alt=Three turtles sit on a dark log surrounded by green lily pads and white flowers in a pond.&gt;&lt;/figure&gt;</content:encoded></item><item><title>Photo of the day for 2025-04-16</title><link>https://rosschurchley.com/2025/animals-ueno-fish/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://rosschurchley.com/2025/animals-ueno-fish/</guid><pubDate>Wed, 16 Apr 2025 23:12:00 GMT</pubDate><content:encoded>&lt;figure&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;/_astro/src.C94EMgOq_22oOuj.webp&quot; width=6000 height=4000 alt=Two fish face the viewer, open mouths poking above the surface.&gt;&lt;/figure&gt;</content:encoded></item><item><title>Photo of the day for 2025-04-15</title><link>https://rosschurchley.com/2025/animals-pig/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://rosschurchley.com/2025/animals-pig/</guid><pubDate>Tue, 15 Apr 2025 23:12:00 GMT</pubDate><content:encoded>&lt;figure&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;/_astro/src.BPPt3eU4_SYozU.webp&quot; width=6000 height=4000 alt=A light grey pig stands in a grassy field, looking directly at the camera with a curious expression.&gt;&lt;/figure&gt;</content:encoded></item><item><title>Watercolour linocut</title><link>https://rosschurchley.com/2025/watercolour-linocut/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://rosschurchley.com/2025/watercolour-linocut/</guid><pubDate>Mon, 14 Apr 2025 23:12:00 GMT</pubDate><content:encoded>&lt;figure&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;/_astro/cover.Ce3N329e_1Sliet.webp&quot; width=2956 height=2217 alt=A seagull in blue ink stamped on top of a watercolour wash suggestive of a cloudy sky&gt;&lt;/figure&gt;&lt;p&gt;A couple weeks ago I did a beginner’s &lt;a href=&quot;https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Linocut&quot;&gt;linocut&lt;/a&gt; workshop at the &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.slicevancouver.ca&quot;&gt;Slice of Life Art Gallery&lt;/a&gt; in East Vancouver. The process was fun and simple: sketch something on tracing paper, transfer the graphite onto a rubber block, then carve out the relief. We stamped our designs on watercolour backgrounds we painted at the start of the workshop.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;gallery-grid&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;gallery-item&quot;&gt;  &lt;img src=&quot;/_astro/IMG_2319.BEREz88N_J9KD0.webp&quot; srcset=&quot;/_astro/IMG_2319.BEREz88N_Z2bbokV.webp 640w, /_astro/IMG_2319.BEREz88N_ZoIds6.webp 750w, /_astro/IMG_2319.BEREz88N_Fdmzt.webp 828w, /_astro/IMG_2319.BEREz88N_Z1ylDmK.webp 1080w, /_astro/IMG_2319.BEREz88N_Z275yOn.webp 1280w, /_astro/IMG_2319.BEREz88N_xnwOL.webp 1668w, /_astro/IMG_2319.BEREz88N_1XWq6s.webp 2048w, /_astro/IMG_2319.BEREz88N_25MNmQ.webp 2560w&quot; alt=&quot;A pencil sketch of a seagull silhouette on a pink rubber block.&quot; loading=&quot;lazy&quot; decoding=&quot;async&quot; sizes=&quot;100vw&quot; data-astro-image=&quot;full-width&quot; data-astro-image-fit=&quot;cover&quot; data-astro-image-pos=&quot;center&quot; width=&quot;2772&quot; height=&quot;2079&quot; class=&quot;gallery-item__image&quot;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;gallery-item&quot;&gt;  &lt;img src=&quot;/_astro/IMG_2328.BNMVTeXZ_Z1rzX0h.webp&quot; srcset=&quot;/_astro/IMG_2328.BNMVTeXZ_2iJBXM.webp 640w, /_astro/IMG_2328.BNMVTeXZ_ZYYkWj.webp 750w, /_astro/IMG_2328.BNMVTeXZ_4Wf5g.webp 828w, /_astro/IMG_2328.BNMVTeXZ_lf7xn.webp 1080w, /_astro/IMG_2328.BNMVTeXZ_ZctMTf.webp 1280w, /_astro/IMG_2328.BNMVTeXZ_2rYiJT.webp 1668w, /_astro/IMG_2328.BNMVTeXZ_Z1bCVMl.webp 2048w, /_astro/IMG_2328.BNMVTeXZ_Z14MyvW.webp 2560w&quot; alt=&quot;A relief carving of a seagull made from a rubber block. The carving has been used as a stamp and has blue ink on it. A pile of pink shavings is in the background.&quot; loading=&quot;lazy&quot; decoding=&quot;async&quot; sizes=&quot;100vw&quot; data-astro-image=&quot;full-width&quot; data-astro-image-fit=&quot;cover&quot; data-astro-image-pos=&quot;center&quot; width=&quot;4032&quot; height=&quot;3024&quot; class=&quot;gallery-item__image&quot;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;I made two designs — a simple seagull on a sky-blue background, and a more experimental depiction of a fire hydrant.&lt;label class=&quot;sidenote-ref&quot; for=&quot;fn-hydrant&quot;&gt;1&lt;/label&gt; I’m quite pleased with how both turned out!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;input class=&quot;sidenote-toggle&quot; id=&quot;fn-hydrant&quot; type=&quot;checkbox&quot;/&gt;
&lt;aside class=&quot;sidenote&quot; data=&quot;1&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Eagle-eyed readers will notice that, although the watercolour gives the vibe of a fire hydrant, the &lt;a href=&quot;/2024/what-colour-is-a-fire-hydrant/&quot;&gt;colour scheme&lt;/a&gt; doesn’t exactly match that of anywhere in BC — all municipalities that have yellow-bodied hydrants with potentially red bonnets would also colour the side caps red. But that wouldn’t have come across in the medium.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/aside&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;gallery-single&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;gallery-item&quot;&gt;  &lt;img src=&quot;/_astro/IMG_2399.DLB13Ir2_1k4kyn.webp&quot; srcset=&quot;/_astro/IMG_2399.DLB13Ir2_1CLit.webp 640w, /_astro/IMG_2399.DLB13Ir2_12prIN.webp 750w, /_astro/IMG_2399.DLB13Ir2_Z13rYW9.webp 828w, /_astro/IMG_2399.DLB13Ir2_2riHnj.webp 1080w, /_astro/IMG_2399.DLB13Ir2_Z1aOSsB.webp 1280w, /_astro/IMG_2399.DLB13Ir2_Z1kSFqI.webp 1668w, /_astro/IMG_2399.DLB13Ir2_25CRdR.webp 2048w&quot; alt=&quot;A black outline of a fire hydrant stamped on a watercolour background that evokes a red and yellow fire hydrant, a blue sky, and green grass.&quot; loading=&quot;lazy&quot; decoding=&quot;async&quot; sizes=&quot;100vw&quot; data-astro-image=&quot;full-width&quot; data-astro-image-fit=&quot;cover&quot; data-astro-image-pos=&quot;center&quot; width=&quot;2374&quot; height=&quot;3324&quot; class=&quot;gallery-item__image&quot;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</content:encoded></item><item><title>Photo of the day for 2025-04-14</title><link>https://rosschurchley.com/2025/animals-crab/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://rosschurchley.com/2025/animals-crab/</guid><pubDate>Mon, 14 Apr 2025 23:12:00 GMT</pubDate><content:encoded>&lt;figure&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;/_astro/src.D2AZiWYA_10okqu.webp&quot; width=6000 height=4000 alt=A dark crab stands on a wet sandy surface, partially submerged in the foam of an incoming wave.&gt;&lt;/figure&gt;</content:encoded></item></channel></rss>